{
  "comment": [
    "Single source for the test262 subset. Each entry maps one shim to the",
    "test262 directories that specify it, plus how to install the shim over",
    "the native so the suite exercises OUR code and not the engine's.",
    "",
    "`install` describes a prototype method or a constructor static:",
    "  target   - the object the method hangs off",
    "  property - the method name test262 calls",
    "  export   - the shim export in the built module",
    "  length   - the method's own `length`, which test262 asserts",
    "  receiverAs - 'argument' passes the receiver as the first parameter,",
    "               'this' invokes the shim with it, absent drops it",
    "",
    "The .gitmodules sparse-checkout must cover every `dirs` entry; the runner",
    "fails loud when it does not."
  ],
  "features": [
    {
      "name": "Array.prototype.toReversed",
      "module": "polyfills/array.js",
      "dirs": ["test/built-ins/Array/prototype/toReversed"],
      "install": {
        "target": "Array.prototype",
        "property": "toReversed",
        "export": "arrayToReversedShim",
        "length": 0,
        "receiverAs": "argument"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Array.prototype.toSorted",
      "module": "polyfills/array.js",
      "dirs": ["test/built-ins/Array/prototype/toSorted"],
      "install": {
        "target": "Array.prototype",
        "property": "toSorted",
        "export": "arrayToSortedShim",
        "length": 1,
        "receiverAs": "argument"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Set.prototype.difference",
      "module": "polyfills/set.js",
      "dirs": ["test/built-ins/Set/prototype/difference"],
      "install": {
        "target": "Set.prototype",
        "property": "difference",
        "export": "setDifferenceShim",
        "length": 1,
        "receiverAs": "argument"
      }
    },
    {
